1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,120
In the last video, K changed with temperature,

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,440
and every K we used was simply given

3
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:06,400
to us.

4
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:08,720
So where do those numbers come from?

5
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:11,680
Nobody can count ions in a test tube.

6
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:14,640
But here is the iron thiocyanate tube again.

7
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:17,840
Iron three plus and thiocyanate join to make

8
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:20,400
F E S C N two plus, an

9
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:22,640
ion that is deep red, and the more

10
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:25,280
of it there is, the deeper the colour.

11
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:27,040
If we could turn that colour into a

12
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:30,520
number, we could measure a concentration at equilibrium,

13
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:32,960
and from that, a real K.

14
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:35,040
So how does a colour reading give you

15
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:35,680
K?

16
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,820
The instrument is a colourimeter.

17
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,540
A lamp shines light through a small clear

18
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:44,580
container of the solution, called a cuvette, and

19
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:46,180
onto a detector.

20
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:48,500
The red ion looks red because it soaks

21
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:51,220
up blue light and lets the red through,

22
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,860
so we set the colourimeter to blue light,

23
00:00:54,060 --> 00:00:56,820
about four hundred and forty-seven nanometres.

24
00:00:56,900 --> 00:00:59,220
The more red ions in the light's path,

25
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:01,540
the more blue light they absorb, and the

26
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:03,620
less reaches the detector.

27
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:07,060
The meter reports this as absorbance, where zero

28
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:09,540
means no light is absorbed.

29
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:11,460
First we put in a cuvette of plain

30
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:14,180
water, the blank, and set it to zero,

31
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:16,340
so the water and the glass don't count.

32
00:01:17,567 --> 00:01:19,206
Here is the useful part.

33
00:01:19,487 --> 00:01:21,086
If the light and the cuvette stay the

34
00:01:21,167 --> 00:01:23,766
same, doubling the number of red ions in

35
00:01:23,807 --> 00:01:26,326
the light's path doubles the absorbance.

36
00:01:26,607 --> 00:01:29,806
Chemists write this as A equals epsilon l

37
00:01:29,967 --> 00:01:30,606
c.

38
00:01:30,927 --> 00:01:34,526
A is the absorbance, c is the concentration,

39
00:01:34,687 --> 00:01:36,286
l is the width of the cuvette the

40
00:01:36,407 --> 00:01:39,086
light travels through, and epsilon is a number

41
00:01:39,167 --> 00:01:41,966
that says how strongly this ion absorbs this

42
00:01:42,167 --> 00:01:42,646
light.

43
00:01:42,927 --> 00:01:45,246
With the same cuvette and the same light,

44
00:01:45,487 --> 00:01:48,766
epsilon and l stay fixed, so absorbance rises

45
00:01:48,847 --> 00:01:50,446
in step with concentration.

46
00:01:51,667 --> 00:01:54,306
To turn a reading into a concentration, we

47
00:01:54,387 --> 00:01:57,186
need solutions where we already know the answer.

48
00:01:57,427 --> 00:01:59,186
These are the standards.

49
00:01:59,267 --> 00:02:01,906
Each one has a measured amount of thiocyanate

50
00:02:01,947 --> 00:02:04,706
and a big excess of iron three plus.

51
00:02:04,787 --> 00:02:07,586
All that extra iron pushes the equilibrium far

52
00:02:07,667 --> 00:02:09,906
to the right, just like adding a reactant

53
00:02:09,947 --> 00:02:13,586
in the disturbance videos, so almost every thiocyanate

54
00:02:13,667 --> 00:02:15,906
ion ends up in the red ion.

55
00:02:16,027 --> 00:02:18,706
That means the red ion's concentration is about

56
00:02:18,787 --> 00:02:22,146
equal to the thiocyanate concentration in that standard,

57
00:02:22,227 --> 00:02:24,146
which we know from how it was made.

58
00:02:24,267 --> 00:02:27,986
Five standards give five known concentrations, from pale

59
00:02:28,067 --> 00:02:28,946
to deep red.

60
00:02:30,167 --> 00:02:32,486
Now measure the absorbance of each standard and

61
00:02:32,647 --> 00:02:35,926
plot it, absorbance up the side and concentration

62
00:02:36,047 --> 00:02:36,806
along the bottom.

63
00:02:37,287 --> 00:02:39,206
The blank gives the point at zero.

64
00:02:39,767 --> 00:02:42,006
The points fall close to a straight line,

65
00:02:42,087 --> 00:02:43,846
so we draw the line of best fit

66
00:02:43,927 --> 00:02:46,046
through them, not dot to dot.

67
00:02:46,327 --> 00:02:48,486
Because we zeroed with the blank, the line

68
00:02:48,567 --> 00:02:50,486
passes very close to the origin.

69
00:02:51,127 --> 00:02:52,566
Why not just use the formula?

70
00:02:52,967 --> 00:02:55,366
The slope you measure depends on this instrument,

71
00:02:55,447 --> 00:02:58,406
its filter and these cuvettes, so a book

72
00:02:58,487 --> 00:03:01,286
value of epsilon won't quite match yours.

73
00:03:01,607 --> 00:03:04,006
Measuring your own standards on the same machine

74
00:03:04,087 --> 00:03:06,966
is the calibration, and the line only applies

75
00:03:07,047 --> 00:03:08,886
inside the range of the standards.

76
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:12,180
Now a real equilibrium.

77
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:18,580
Mix 5.00 millilitres of 0.00200 moles

78
00:03:18,660 --> 00:03:23,060
per litre iron three plus with 5.00 millilitres

79
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:28,100
of 0.00200 moles per litre thiocyanate.

80
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:31,060
This time neither is in excess, so the

81
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:34,100
mixture settles with all three ions present, and

82
00:03:34,180 --> 00:03:36,340
nobody knows how much red ion there is.

83
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:38,180
That is what we measure.

84
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:41,900
Its absorbance is 0.705.

85
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:45,780
Go across from 0.705 to the line, then

86
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:50,260
straight down to the concentration axis: 1.50 times

87
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:52,780
ten to the minus four moles per litre.

88
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,540
If you are given the line's equation instead,

89
00:03:55,620 --> 00:03:58,740
subtract the intercept from both sides, then divide

90
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:00,660
both sides by the gradient, and you get

91
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:01,700
the same value.

92
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:05,340
Before the ICE table, one trap.

93
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:10,660
The bottles were 0.00200 moles per litre,

94
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:13,620
but pouring 5 millilitres into a 10 millilitre

95
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:17,380
total spreads each ion through twice the volume.

96
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:23,540
So each starting concentration halves: 0.00200 times

97
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:29,860
5.00 over 10.00 is 0.00100

98
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:33,700
moles per litre, for iron and for thiocyanate.

99
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:37,460
Always use the concentrations after mixing, never the

100
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:38,500
bottle values.

101
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:42,340
Now the ICE table from earlier: I for

102
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:46,260
initial, C for change, and E for equilibrium.

103
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:51,780
The initial row is 0.00100 for iron,

104
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:56,420
0.00100 for thiocyanate, and zero for

105
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:57,220
the red ion.

106
00:04:57,860 --> 00:05:00,260
The measured value goes in the equilibrium row

107
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:04,020
first: 1.50 times ten to the minus four

108
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:05,260
for the red ion.

109
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:09,460
Its change is equilibrium minus initial, so plus

110
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:12,660
1.50 times ten to the minus four.

111
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:15,860
The equation is one to one to one,

112
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,500
so iron and thiocyanate each fall by the

113
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:19,700
same amount.

114
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:22,660
That leaves 8.50 times ten to the minus

115
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:24,740
four of each at equilibrium.

116
00:05:25,967 --> 00:05:29,726
Now substitute the equilibrium values into the expression:

117
00:05:29,767 --> 00:05:33,006
the red ion over iron times thiocyanate.

118
00:05:33,487 --> 00:05:36,606
That is 1.50 times ten to the minus

119
00:05:36,767 --> 00:05:40,206
four, over 8.50 times ten to the minus

120
00:05:40,287 --> 00:05:44,046
four squared, which gives about 208, with no

121
00:05:44,127 --> 00:05:44,766
unit written.

122
00:05:45,727 --> 00:05:48,166
Notice what that number does not mean.

123
00:05:48,447 --> 00:05:51,006
Only fifteen percent of the iron became the

124
00:05:51,087 --> 00:05:53,726
red ion, so K in the hundreds does

125
00:05:53,887 --> 00:05:56,166
not mean almost all products.

126
00:05:56,447 --> 00:05:57,886
It sits in the middle band from the

127
00:05:57,967 --> 00:06:01,006
expressions video, with all three ions present in

128
00:06:01,087 --> 00:06:02,286
measurable amounts.

129
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:05,260
One mixture is not enough.

130
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,380
A class makes five mixtures with different starting

131
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:11,340
amounts and measures each at the same temperature.

132
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:14,540
If K really is constant, the five values

133
00:06:14,620 --> 00:06:17,420
should agree, and here they come out between

134
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:22,380
205 and 214, with an average of 208.

135
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:24,620
That spread tells you how far to trust

136
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:25,820
the result.

137
00:06:25,940 --> 00:06:28,460
Write the temperature beside it, because K changes

138
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:29,900
with temperature.

139
00:06:29,940 --> 00:06:32,940
The weak points are measuring small volumes, how

140
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:35,340
well the line fits, and the assumption that

141
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:38,700
the standards turned almost all their thiocyanate red.

142
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:41,020
Two lines to keep.

143
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:44,620
First, measure the colour it absorbs, not the

144
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:47,660
colour you see: a red solution is read

145
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:48,620
with blue light.

146
00:06:49,260 --> 00:06:54,140
Second, the chain: standards, graph, reading, ICE

147
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:55,340
table, K.

148
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:58,020
Each step feeds the next one, and the

149
00:06:58,060 --> 00:07:01,020
dilution comes just before the ICE table.

150
00:07:02,234 --> 00:07:03,113
Your turn.

151
00:07:03,354 --> 00:07:06,033
Same calibration graph, same temperature.

152
00:07:06,234 --> 00:07:12,713
A new mixture: 4.50 millilitres of 0.00200 moles

153
00:07:12,794 --> 00:07:17,193
per litre iron three plus, 3.50 millilitres of

154
00:07:17,314 --> 00:07:21,833
0.00200 moles per litre thiocyanate,

155
00:07:21,954 --> 00:07:24,953
and 2.00 millilitres of water.

156
00:07:25,274 --> 00:07:28,713
Its absorbance is 0.470.

157
00:07:28,874 --> 00:07:29,513
Find K.

158
00:07:30,074 --> 00:07:31,353
Pause here to answer.

159
00:07:41,767 --> 00:07:44,006
The answer is about 208.

160
00:07:44,647 --> 00:07:49,366
First, dilute: in 10.00 millilitres,

161
00:07:49,447 --> 00:07:52,806
iron starts at 9.00 times ten to the

162
00:07:52,967 --> 00:07:57,206
minus four and thiocyanate at 7.00 times ten

163
00:07:57,287 --> 00:07:58,726
to the minus four.

164
00:07:58,887 --> 00:08:03,686
Then read across from 0.470 and down: 1.00

165
00:08:03,767 --> 00:08:06,366
times ten to the minus four of the

166
00:08:06,407 --> 00:08:07,286
red ion.

167
00:08:07,527 --> 00:08:10,086
That goes in the equilibrium row first, so

168
00:08:10,207 --> 00:08:12,966
each reactant falls by the same amount, leaving

169
00:08:13,047 --> 00:08:17,126
8.00 and 6.00 times ten to the minus

170
00:08:17,207 --> 00:08:18,006
four.

171
00:08:18,087 --> 00:08:21,126
Divide, and K is about 208.

172
00:08:21,207 --> 00:08:23,446
That's the same K from a different mixture,

173
00:08:23,567 --> 00:08:26,126
because K stays constant at one temperature.

174
00:08:26,407 --> 00:08:28,526
If you got about 28, you used the

175
00:08:28,567 --> 00:08:31,366
bottle concentrations, so dilute first.

176
00:08:32,567 --> 00:08:35,926
So, to get K from colour: make standards

177
00:08:36,047 --> 00:08:38,886
with one reactant in big excess, plot the

178
00:08:38,967 --> 00:08:42,566
calibration line, read the mixture's absorbance across and

179
00:08:42,767 --> 00:08:46,486
down, work out the starting concentrations after mixing,

180
00:08:46,567 --> 00:08:48,886
put the measured value in the equilibrium row

181
00:08:49,127 --> 00:08:51,126
first, then substitute.

182
00:08:51,287 --> 00:08:53,406
And always record the temperature.

183
00:08:53,847 --> 00:08:57,046
Next: two K values with their own names,

184
00:08:57,127 --> 00:09:00,246
Ka and Kb, for acids and bases.

185
00:09:01,467 --> 00:09:02,906
Here are the key notes.

186
00:09:03,147 --> 00:09:05,066
Pause the video if you need more time

187
00:09:05,147 --> 00:09:05,946
to copy them.
